cycling groups and bike shops all across  the valley are also just  reeling from this tragedy today those  killed and those  injured this morning known to many as  very experienced  and very talented riders arko mana  joining us now live tonight just outside  of a las vegas city cyclery  near twain and town center with how the  community is reacting and remembering  those involved orca  well denise this is a devastating loss  for the local cycling community when a  cyclist dies in a vehicle crash  sculptures like this one  here in front of las vegas likely are  put up to honor them at the general  manager telling me  those who lost their lives today will  never be forgotten  we're just all numb we're just we're  processing it it's  it's been tough sean tyrone is at a loss  for words  he tells me some of his friends and  cycling buddies tragically died in  thursday's crash on the 95.  it's a pain the whole las vegas cycling  community is feeling right now  we're a tight-knit group here in town it  affects all of us as cyclists  personally you know we're all out there  every day you know enjoying our hobby  and and trying to  you know stay alive shawn is the general  manager at las vegas cyclery where this  ghost bike sculpture sits  he expects to see one at the site of  thursday's crash as these white bikes  are usually placed where cyclists have  died in car crashes  to raise awareness and just to remind  everyone that you know  there's not a text or a phone call or  anything  distraction wise that's worth somebody's  life the bike industry in las vegas is  definitely  hurting today dan county with mcgee's  bike shop tells me some of the people  killed were customers here and although  it's still unclear what exactly caused  the box truck to veer into the cyclists  one thing is for certain these were  highly skilled and safe riders  it sounds like everybody was doing the  right thing everybody was they had a  vehicle with them  maintaining a safe distance you know  